# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not tidiness. The dashboard is served under a content policy that
# allows its inline script by sha256 hash, and the HTML parser normalises CRLF
# to LF before it hashes anything — so a CRLF checkout produces a file whose
# bytes hash differently from what the browser will hash. server.mjs normalises
# before hashing so it is correct either way, but leaving the working tree
# consistent removes the whole class of problem rather than compensating for it.
#
# It also keeps the sha256 in RELEASE.json meaningful: the receipt records the
# bytes of a built page, and those bytes should not depend on which machine
# checked the template out.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
